End-to-End Flow (Current)
 
Data Workflow and Process (Narrative)
1.	Runner loads candidate rows and filters out removed candidates.
2.	Runner enriches unit context from EV event/equipment and IBAT lookups.
3.	Runner loads TIL profile and optional document text/table context.
4.	Information-only gate runs first.
5.	Template coverage stage runs for non-information-only rows.
6.	If template is fully covered (no gaps), row stops before completion/applicability.
7.	Otherwise, service-history evidence retrieval and completion review run.
8.	SBOM context is built from profile keys and matched ESN.
9.	Final case payload is assembled with all context lanes.
10.	Final applicability LLM generates verdict and reasoning fields.
11.	Runner writes summary, line-item exports, prompt payload artifacts, and markdown companions.
Inputs
Primary run inputs:
•	candidate CSV from Step 6 candidate pool pipeline
•	optional profile cache directory (til_profile_pilot_*)
•	optional TIL document extraction modes and limits
•	prompt pack and optional system prompt file
•	retrieval depth hints for service-history stage
Data sources used by the run:
•	Databricks EV and unit context tables
•	TIL PDF sources (volume, local sample, SQL fallback)
•	FSR and ER evidence retrieval backends
•	Primavera template activity sources
•	SBOM SOT and sample fallback workbooks
Outputs and Artifacts
Per-run output folder includes:
•	summary workbook and CSV views
•	records.jsonl and payload snapshots
•	completion line-item CSV
•	template line-item CSV
•	prompt inputs/prompts/artifact sheets
•	run markdown companions for summary and context artifacts
•	template coverage records artifact
Key exported fields include:
•	pipeline and final disposition
•	template coverage class and status
•	prior service evidence and completion review metrics
•	SBOM status and evidence fields
•	LLM verdict, confidence, and evidence snippets
Preliminary Experiment Findings
1.	E6.6 runner is now a multi-stage orchestration, not a single final-LLM step.
2.	Skip pathways (information_only_skip, template_covered_skip) reduce unnecessary downstream work.
3.	Service-history lane has policy-aware retrieval depth behavior for recurring and non-recurring completion patterns.
4.	SBOM lane is integrated as supporting configuration evidence with deterministic matching.
5.	Final payload and exports are rich enough for post-run QA and SME walkthroughs.
Known Gaps and Uncertainties for Runtime/Production
1.	Environment dependency:
•	Databricks permissions and source availability can still block parts of the flow.
1.	Cross-lane calibration:
•	interactions between template coverage, completion review, and final verdict need continued SME calibration.
1.	Prior-outage scoping context:
•	design logic is documented, but full runtime integration is still a planned implementation slice.
1.	Quality governance:
•	run-level quality KPIs and acceptance thresholds are not yet formalized for production readiness.
1.	Operational hardening:
•	retry/fallback behavior exists but centralized health checks and source readiness checks are still limited.
What This End-to-End Stage Should and Should Not Decide
Should decide:
•	structured, evidence-aware recommendation support for Step 6 disposition evaluation
•	whether a row should be skipped, reviewed as net-new, or flagged as uncertain
Should not decide:
•	absolute proof of implementation completion from one evidence source
•	hard exclusions based on single missing signals (for example, no SBOM match only)
